First, let us say "[Welcome to Buttondown](/welcome-to-buttondown)!" This guide will walk you through your options for moving your subscribers and campaigns from Mailchimp to Buttondown.

Before we get started, a quick note about terminology:

| Mailchimp    | Buttondown   | Description                                                                 |
|------------------|------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Contacts         | Subscribers      | People who receive your emails.                                             |
| Campaigns        | Archives         | Sent email newsletters or campaigns.                                        |
| Audience         | Newsletter             | A group of contacts/subscribers.                                            |
| Merge Tags       | Metadata    | Personalized fields (like first name) in emails.                            |


## Importing automatically (recommended)

If you tell Buttondown you're coming from Mailchimp when you sign up, you'll see a **Connect Mailchimp** button in your onboarding checklist. Click it, authorize Buttondown in Mailchimp, and we'll automatically bring over your subscribers (grouped by audience, with their tags intact) and your sent campaigns — no exports or file uploads needed.

If you'd rather move your data over by hand, the export-and-upload process below works too.

## Importing manually
### Exporting your subscribers (contacts) from Mailchimp

Export your Mailchimp contacts by following the process in [Mailchimp's documentation](https://mailchimp.com/help/view-export-contacts/).

### Importing your subscribers to Buttondown

Navigate to the "[Subscribers](https://buttondown.com/subscribers)" tab of your Buttondown dashboard to complete the import process.

To learn more, read [Importing your subscribers](/importing-your-data#importing-your-subscribers).

### Exporting your archives (campaigns) from Mailchimp

To [export your Mailchimp campaigns](https://mailchimp.com/help/export-back-up-data/), go to Account → Settings → Manage my data. Then click "Export my data". This will download a ZIP file containing all of your sent campaigns.

Once you have the ZIP file, go to the Buttondown dashboard and open the "[Emails](https://buttondown.com/emails)" tab. Click **Import**, select "Mailchimp", then upload the ZIP file you just downloaded from Mailchimp.

After you complete the steps above, Buttondown begins an audit and migration process to make sure everything is in order. Once that's done, you're free to disable or deactivate your Mailchimp account.

